# Voice Typer — keyboard event device access
#
# Grants read access to keyboard event devices for members of the "input"
# group. Installed by the Voice Typer package (or via pkexec for AppImage
# users). Do not edit — remove this file to revoke access.
#
# Why MODE="0660" + GROUP="input": owner (root) gets rw, group (input)
# gets rw, others get nothing. This is the standard pattern for /dev/input
# access (same as the docker group for /var/run/docker.sock).
#
# Why ENV{ID_INPUT_KEYBOARD}=="?*": narrows the rule to
# keyboard-class devices only (set by udev's input_id builtin). Without
# this guard, the rule would also relax permissions on mice, joysticks,
# touchscreens and other non-keyboard event devices — a privilege
# escalation surface unrelated to Voice Typer's needs.
#
# Why no RUN+="...udevadm trigger...": modern udev (systemd ≥ 183)
# applies rules at device-creation time automatically — an explicit
# ``udevadm trigger`` on ``ACTION=="add"`` is redundant and causes a
# recursive trigger storm on some kernels. The ``udevadm control
# --reload-rules && udevadm trigger --subsystem-match=input`` run by
# install_permissions.py after copying this file is sufficient for both
# already-plugged-in devices and future hotplugs.

# Match keyboard-class input event devices only.
KERNEL=="event[0-9]*", SUBSYSTEM=="input", ENV{ID_INPUT_KEYBOARD}=="?*", GROUP="input", MODE="0660"
